=== Pterosaur research ===
* Walters, [[Emily Rayfield|Rayfield]] & [[Philip Donoghue|Donoghue]] (2026) argue that modern reconstructions of pterosaur wings likely underestimate the diversity of wing shapes within this group.<ref>{{cite journal|last1=Walters |first1=B. |last2=Rayfield |first2=E. J. |last3=Donoghue |first3=P. C. J. |year=2026 |title=Exploring the limits of wing design in pterosaurs |journal=Paleobiology |volume=52 |issue=3 |pages=495–506 |doi=10.1017/pab.2026.10103 |doi-access=free |bibcode=2026Pbio...52..495W }}</ref>
* Ji (2026) describes a partial skeleton of an indeterminate pterosaur, marking the first record of the group from the Mazongshan Dinosaur Fauna ([[Xiagou Formation]], China).<ref name="J26">{{cite journal |last1=Ji |first1=Shu'an |title=First discovery of the Early Cretaceous pterosaur from western Gansu Province and supplement to the Mazongshan Dinosaur Fauna |url=https://www.sciengine.com/GeoBullChina/doi/10.12097/gbc.2023.08.034 |journal=Geological Bulletin of China |date=2026 |volume=45 |issue=7 |pages=1374–1382 |doi=10.12097/gbc.2023.08.034 |doi-broken-date=27 September 2026 }}</ref>

